    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "2086831138841211056",
      "url": "https://x.com/advaith_sridhar/status/2086831138841211056",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/advaith_sridhar/status/2086831138841211056",
      "text": "Semiconductor chips are bottlenecked by heat, and better materials would enable dramatic improvements in chip performance. For example, new thermally conductive dielectric materials would make chips 10x more energy efficient by enabling 3D packaging of logic and memory. Several other parts of AI chips - the substrates, interconnects, or the transistor itself - require new materials to push chip performance.",
      "source": "Twitter Web App",
